        "text": "Sunlight contains all visible colors. As it passes through the atmosphere, tiny air molecules scatter shorter wavelengths much more strongly than longer ones\u2014a process called **Rayleigh scattering**. Blue light is scattered across the sky, so it reaches your eyes from many directions.\n\nViolet is scattered even more, but the Sun emits less of it, and our eyes are less sensitive to violet, so the sky appears blue rather than violet. The ocean isn\u2019t what makes it blue.",
